On Sat, Nov 15, 2014 at 8:32 PM, John Cowan <cowan@mercury.ccil.org> wrote:

> Jorge Llamb=C3=ADas scripsit:
>
> > The rule for fu'ivla rafsi is also simple in principle: drop the final
> > vowel and replace it with y (just as with gismu),
>
> Such fu'ivla rafsi are irredeemably ambiguous anyway, since there is no
> constraint against having two fu'ivla that differ only in the final vowel=
.
>

True. In practice we don't seem to have many fu'ivla that differ only in
the final vowel, but in principle these rafsi are ambiguous. CLL mentions
CCVVCV as a fu'ivla form that could have this type of rafsi. Other obvious
forms are any fu'ivla that begins with a vowel and ends in CV (such as
".esporte") or any fu'ivla containing a consonantal syllable and ending in
CV, which includes all the type-3 that end in CV.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

